SUBJECTIVE

Chief Complaint: I can't stop throwing up, my chest is tight, and I feel like the ground has completely opened up underneath me.
History of Present Illness: The patient describes a history of profound grief over the loss of a previously sustaining faith community, leading to an ongoing existential vacuum following the deconstruction of a fundamentalist worldview. Tonight, while walking past a building affiliated with their former religion, the patient experienced an intense trigger response to the religious symbols, culminating in a severe panic attack and intractable vomiting. The patient reports deep-seated internalized shame regarding their identity (which was weaponized by religious doctrine), strained relationships with family members remaining in the exclusionary faith, and hyper-sensitivity to perceived manipulation. They note chronic anger toward the hypocrisy of the exclusionary institution and difficulty trusting their own intuition after years of institutional gaslighting.
Functional Status: Acutely functionally impaired; confined to the bathroom, unable to retain fluids or stand due to severe panic and retching.
Social/Safety Concerns: High risk of profound social isolation and severe metabolic derangement due to the physical severity of the trauma responses.

