ASSESSMENT

Primary Diagnosis: Spiritual Trauma from Exclusionary Institutions - Other Specified Trauma/Stressor Disorder - V62.89 (Religious or spiritual problem) - Status: Exacerbated
Differentials:

Acute Gastroenteritis / Food Poisoning - Ruled out/unlikely due to the abrupt onset precisely linked to a known psychological trauma trigger, the absence of diarrhea or fever, and the prominent hyperventilation.

Peptic Ulcer Disease / Biliary Colic - Ruled out/unlikely as the abdomen remains soft without focal right upper quadrant or severe retrosternal pain, and the tenderness is purely mechanical from the act of vomiting.

Panic Disorder - Ruled out/unlikely as the primary diagnosis because the severe autonomic arousal and somatic symptoms are strictly context-dependent and triggered exclusively by specific institutional trauma cues, rather than spontaneous panic attacks.
